tion":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5d32fdc3c560613e2cf8c370a2012d9fa4cb27944c4f756bb175824b74d734b7","compact":"92e56a55cc4c40d87d64cc2e4769b7f90e08fd40bc3501dcb2637e120dd04caf","nasal":"8061a85f0a2fc33a89df2908cb83432314f4468d55e44197b00b219e793be0a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":7,"english":"That conqueror in battle, Ravana's son, with shafts sorely pierced the persons of Rāma and Laksmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.792,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"794a9d4e5e8ec83b978354e13b36ad96b7b09b474e8dafca21249dde68816d07","compact":"ae4afe933d56be861f447a46ca3fc2beafeb533c0133727d082bd2fc3e493520","nasal":"ae4afe933d56be861f447a46ca3fc2beafeb533c0133727d082bd2fc3e493520"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":8,"english":"And both Rāma and Lakşmaņa had their bodies entirely covered by the angry Indrajit with shafts turned into serpents.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.641,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f41d4a70cc916e46b659f8d9c2e20da2eda2375188101198c8abaf53c6fda55b","compact":"9021b66d5f30a66e97d3d7f3ee183e3e9da6463923a4e7762c3275b9a2aa1912","nasal":"7670e66997944bda3d005fb7a299e7cd573033f5526b33856a1da90cdeaf45ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":9,"english":"And from their wounds blood began to gush out in streams; and they looked like flowercrowned Kinsukas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"45a60bd626dfa256e222fb0ee9431607699bd82bf6a4b96a8233bdc7b3cc03aa","compact":"b31b215618fdbdd449960783e1c4759b6896ccd0fd2d5cd4eae1754a381620a7","nasal":"b31b215618fdbdd449960783e1c4759b6896ccd0fd2d5cd4eae1754a381620a7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":10,"english":"Then that one having red corners to his eyes and resembling a mass of crushed collyrium, Rāvana's son, said to the brothers, as he vanished.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.848,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"91bcbc03af115041ad09ad92fe73394b250c39fcd4b40c0ab9263225e22fcc3f","compact":"b2d7b576ba5c52a70708269b08fe14bbd29ba9c479506fa133c3894e5ff24f28","nasal":"3d2106ea58318e85854faaa39dc6801c5c8afb084c5f085378aa9009d8609fbc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":11,"english":"When I fight remaining invisible, even Sakrathe lord of the celestials-cannot see or approach me, and who are you?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eaf5bdf4ce65e0dbaf276ce387b27128861b3c292466500f4e8d8f46d2b42c5d","compact":"771fe8637881a0eb0d460399dfdd13022fabd7564ca168bd0a9befa9401b1d01","nasal":"771fe8637881a0eb0d460399dfdd13022fabd7564ca168bd0a9befa9401b1d01"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":12,"english":"And I, with my soul surcharged with wrath, shall, assailing them with showers of weapons furnished with Karka feathers, send Raghu's sons to the abode of Yama.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d8b60219977860c4ee2f279d00791bbbd6cff2038943ca0290e6c97a481f6c27","compact":"5ce6b84fb6536b58451963168c799c2a0a51f38ef37a54e887a0097aa8274a53","nasal":"948420d463ee3285d7fd09358a3f4cd1054086878b53039c45624fbc17f3f8ab"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":13,"english":"Having spoken thus to the brothers-Rāma and Laksmana, cognizant of righteousness-(Indrajit)pierced them with sharpened shafts, and shouted in joy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1b3c16bc7329d4d8107eb5697322047fa7311ea3cbdf66e078c1ee26cb340146","compact":"f1c74151f92956192bde9db12c451fa668ee0750454a7dc718c94572836c43a5","nasal":"f1c74151f92956192bde9db12c451fa668ee0750454a7dc718c94572836c43a5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":14,"english":"And stretching his large bow, that one sable like to a mass of crushed collyrium again discharged terrific shafts in battle.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a195d41108ee9c8bdb031bc610106e610b67be41eff6018ba31626c00296f3c4","compact":"24b5d374cdb95a872c48d846f044f6ffe81bc7debee300074747787428bcc98c","nasal":"ef7379efb803a1a0b2facb3c226612f7cd2d5fca7636739148dadcb761e91cc3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":15,"english":"That one versed in the inner sense of things, with whetted arrows pierced the vitals of Rāma and Lakşmaņa and shouted momentarily.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"555dad7b2b90380d5821bb5d16968bef54db67a9bcb48ad3d65715cc72bf8100","compact":"5ff459998d7762f85886d34d6f952f8bcbb713aa8a28be079b262f527a771239","nasal":"0ae4d397dbd1ca6d6246ae6d29b7cd05355b78beeacec7a94e2f175cc66dd5f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":16,"english":"And fast bound by the shackles of shafts on the edge of battle, they* could not attain respite for a moment, *i.e. Rama and Laksmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.828,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4989c333639e46e234e62b449ffedb07fd2b3708eb1d93779f63c01d0abd8af7","compact":"d20382ac3188adf3699945d41d9256fc8d9f4c8bf048d6df0f4ed0c4eb57d26d","nasal":"0e5f3d4596909adeabb088026730297c4edea48289ff143b115f73dce6abdc44"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-35-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":35,"verse":17,"english":"Then with their persons pierced with shafts and darts, and resembling the flags of the Great Indra let loose from the cords and trembling (in the air), and with their bodies bristling with arrows, those heroes and mighty bowmen-lords of the earth-tormented in consequence of their vitals having been pierced, dropped down to the earth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-45-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6035017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d14093dae58205c0718c41273022e6c05a8dc55ff68f215122a0e7